 "about_text": "Misa Shin Gallery opened in November 2010 in Shirokane, Tokyo, in a former ironworks building, and relocated in August 2018 to Minamiazabu, a quiet residential district near several embassies. The gallery presents exhibitions of Japanese and international artists working with a conceptual approach, giving particular attention to mid-career artists and to Japanese conceptualism of the 1960s and 1970s, aiming to reassess this postwar history for international audiences. Beyond its exhibition program, the gallery advises corporate art collections and art programs in Japan and has been involved in public art projects in Zhengzhou, China, and Doha, Qatar. It also explores connections between art and other disciplines such as architecture, theater and music.",
